        <mxCell id="c114" value="Memo" style="rounded=0;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F2F3F4;strokeColor=#D5D8DC;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#2C3E50;fontSize=12;fontStyle=0;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="166" y="490" width="70" height="24" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c115" value="&lt;i&gt;Outlined in teal: the five components. Outlined in coral: the proposed rate, B10, their sum (its formula is in the bar). Below it come the labor-content case with no indirect hours, the current standard (the conversion released per standard hour), the time-driven rate, the base year&#x27;s actual cost per standard hour, and the proposed rate with supervision and depreciation spread over 90% and 110% of the plan volume, the ends of the normal-capacity range. Labels are wrapped here, as the workbook wraps a long label within column A. Columns J to Q hold the Table OnHand and are not shown.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="520" width="860" height="68" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
